# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated caches (Rt bootstrapping is slow; results are reproducible)
Code/results/_cache/

# Sweep checkpoints. The horizon-1 checkpoints stay committed; a full sweep is
# 5 horizons x 12 experiments of weights that any run reproduces from scratch.
Code/checkpoints/horizon_*/

# Backtest and sweep output. A rolling backtest is 4 seasons x 3 horizons x
# every arm; at ~300 KB of predictions/metrics per run that is gigabytes, and
# any run reproduces it from the recorded seed and config. The per-run trees
# are ignored, except what the paper reads (below). The aggregated
# _backtest/ tables are committed.
Code/results/backtest_*/**
!Code/results/backtest_*/**/

# Exception: the paper's inputs (see Paper/scripts/README.md). Boston's 3
# unseen seasons: the week-level tests and the run files (predictions, metrics,
# settings) of every model the paper reports, plus the compute table. ~60 MB.
# Columbus and Chicago results live under Code/results/<city>/ and are tracked.
!Code/results/backtest_202[2-4]_2[3-5]/horizon_*/_comparison/*.csv
!Code/results/backtest_202[2-4]_2[3-5]/horizon_*/gnn_st_tuned/*/*
!Code/results/backtest_202[2-4]_2[3-5]/horizon_*/gnn_st_nograph_tuned/*/*
